    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `get_positive` Python function:\n\n```python\ndef # get_positive(l: list) -> # list:\n    # Return only positive numbers.\n\n    \"\"\"Return only positive numbers in the list.\n    >>> get_positive([-1, 2, -4, 5, 6])\n    [2, 5, 6]\n    >>> get_positive([5, 3, -5, 2, -3, 3, 9, 0, 123, 1, -10])\n    [5, 3, 2, 3, 9, 123, 1]\n    \"\"\"\n    return [num for num in l if num > 0]\n```\n\nThis function uses a list comprehension to create a new list that includes only the strictly positive numbers from the input list `l`. The docstring provides examples for the function.",
